        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03393-2">
            <title>[7] Superconductivity with a squeeze</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03393-2</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> Michael E. Ziebel</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 7/10</span> <b>B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> News coverage of heavy-fermion superconductivity in a novel van der Waals material</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#material</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#vanderWaals</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#heavyfermion</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#superconductivity</span></p><p><img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03393-2/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3393_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> Heavy-fermion superconductivity has now been observed under pressure in the van der Waals metal CeSiI. This material will provide a new platform for studying the interplay of dimensionality and Kondo physics.</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title>[7] Superconductivity with a squeeze</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Michael E. Ziebel</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03393-2</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Physics, Published online: 2026-07-28; | doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03393-2</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-07-28</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Physics</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/s41567-026-03393-2</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03393-2</prism:url>
        <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Last authors:&lt;/b&gt; Michael E. Ziebel&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'&gt;Score 7/10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;b&gt;B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; News coverage of heavy-fermion superconductivity in a novel van der Waals material&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#material&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#vanderWaals&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#heavyfermion&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#superconductivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03393-2/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3393_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; Heavy-fermion superconductivity has now been observed under pressure in the van der Waals metal CeSiI. This material will provide a new platform for studying the interplay of dimensionality and Kondo physics.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
    
        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03392-3">
            <title>[8] Superconductivity under pressure in a van der Waals heavy-fermion metal</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03392-3</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> Hechang Lei, Jinguang Cheng</p><p><b>Authors:</b> Tong Shi, Wenhao Li, Qingxin Dong, et al.</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 8/10</span> <b>B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> Discovery of unconventional superconductivity and Kondo physics in a 2D van der Waals material</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#material</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#vanderWaals</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#heavyfermion</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#superconductivity</span></p><p><img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03392-3/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3392_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> CeSiI is a two-dimensional heavy-fermion metal. Now, the interplay between antiferromagnetism, Kondo coherence and unconventional superconductivity is observed by applying pressure to this material.</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title>[8] Superconductivity under pressure in a van der Waals heavy-fermion metal</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Last authors: Hechang Lei, Jinguang Cheng; Authors: Tong Shi, Wenhao Li, Qingxin Dong, et al.</dc:creator><dc:creator>Wenhao Li</dc:creator><dc:creator>Qingxin Dong</dc:creator><dc:creator>Pengtao Yang</dc:creator><dc:creator>Hanming Ma</dc:creator><dc:creator>Zhaoming Tian</dc:creator><dc:creator>Ningning Wang</dc:creator><dc:creator>Jianping Sun</dc:creator><dc:creator>Yoshiya Uwatoko</dc:creator><dc:creator>Yi-feng Yang</dc:creator><dc:creator>Bosen Wang</dc:creator><dc:creator>Hechang Lei</dc:creator><dc:creator>Jinguang Cheng</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03392-3</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Physics, Published online: 2026-07-28; | doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03392-3</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-07-28</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Physics</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/s41567-026-03392-3</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03392-3</prism:url>
        <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Last authors:&lt;/b&gt; Hechang Lei, Jinguang Cheng&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Authors:&lt;/b&gt; Tong Shi, Wenhao Li, Qingxin Dong, et al.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'&gt;Score 8/10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;b&gt;B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; Discovery of unconventional superconductivity and Kondo physics in a 2D van der Waals material&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#material&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#vanderWaals&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#heavyfermion&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#superconductivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03392-3/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3392_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; CeSiI is a two-dimensional heavy-fermion metal. Now, the interplay between antiferromagnetism, Kondo coherence and unconventional superconductivity is observed by applying pressure to this material.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
    
        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03372-7">
            <title>[9] A magnetic impurity sets off ripples in a kagome superconductor</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03372-7</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> Barun Ghosh</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 9/10</span> <b>A_MUST_READ</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> title strong match: kagome superconductor</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#kagome</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#Kondo</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#superconduct</span></p><p><img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03372-7/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3372_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> The role of magnetic impurities in shaping superconductivity and electronic order in kagome metals remains unresolved. Now, a study reveals anisotropic Kondo resonances intertwined with the superconducting gap in a magnetically doped kagome superconductor.</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title>[9] A magnetic impurity sets off ripples in a kagome superconductor</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Barun Ghosh</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03372-7</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Physics, Published online: 2026-07-22; | doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03372-7</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-07-22</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Physics</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/s41567-026-03372-7</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03372-7</prism:url>
        <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Last authors:&lt;/b&gt; Barun Ghosh&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'&gt;Score 9/10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;b&gt;A_MUST_READ&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; title strong match: kagome superconductor&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#kagome&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#Kondo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#superconduct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03372-7/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3372_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; The role of magnetic impurities in shaping superconductivity and electronic order in kagome metals remains unresolved. Now, a study reveals anisotropic Kondo resonances intertwined with the superconducting gap in a magnetically doped kagome superconductor.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
    
